Third-party code
----------------
None. jarvan-memory is written from scratch and uses only the Python
standard library.

Acknowledgements
----------------
The optional session-summary module (a detached `claude -p` call that writes
session summaries into a daily/ folder) follows the general design of
avenoxbeyin, an MIT-licensed project, Copyright (c) 2026 Avenox. No source
code from that project is included here; the summary, locking and process
handling code in jarvan_memory/jobs.py and jarvan_memory/util.py, and the
Turkish stemmer in jarvan_memory/stem_tr.py, are independent implementations.
